  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p><strong>Tickanetley Bald</strong> rises to 3,967 feet in Georgia.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>This trail is hikeable most of the year. Summer brings heat and humidity \u2014 carry extra water \u2014 while fall and spring offer the most comfortable conditions. Ice is possible on shaded stretches in mid-winter.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include Rich Mountain, Big Bald Mountain and Cowpen Mountain \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
